#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:143
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A PR owner who stalled: tell the owner, then take the stalled PR over."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:137
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train, merges directly. A workflow PR needs no approval beyond the batch card (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Workflow PRs, A)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:132
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Add the merge-train label instead of merging; the train lands the batch with one CI run."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:99
#. Diagram label
msgid "All green per rule 1?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:71
#. Diagram label
msgid "Announce the hand-over or the lapse"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Approve the batch card"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Approves in the merge manager's session only, one card per batch. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Do not merge. The next wake reads the checks again."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Enforce the pacing rule of continual-progress (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Cancel CI): close superseded or duplicate PRs, such as a re-pin whose commits another open PR already carries, and cancel their runs; cancel stale queued runs that never started, never a main push run that has started; ask the owners of P3 PRs to return them to draft."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every check run on the head SHA has finished, and anything pending blocks; wait for every tier, e2e included. The full tier ran (the No new failures judge, or every full test shard); a draft or fast-tier-only pass never counts. Every judge passes (owner ruling, 2026-11-07): an aggregate job covers only the parts it names, and each test shard's own no-new-failures table lists 0 new failures; with no judge, each check concluded success, skipped or neutral. A cancelled job counts only when a later run of the same workflow on the same head passed that job. merge:watch prints this verdict per PR."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "In the merge manager's session only: one card per batch, naming each PR, after its six lines were posted in that chat. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B)."
msgstr ""

