msgid "Pre-approved?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read live, never from a stored copy: the open PRs (draft, head, mergeable, owed checks, open owner decisions), the queued and running runs with the age of the oldest, the latest main push run, and each PR owner's last push or comment. One sweep runs merge:watch over every repository it holds. Liveness duty: acknowledge each new merge request within holding.heartbeatMinutes, and post a heartbeat with each sweep, so siblings can tell a live merge manager from a stalled one."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:58
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the queue, acknowledge requests"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:166
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:88
#. Diagram label
msgid "Relieve the runners"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:123
#. Diagram label
msgid "Rides the train?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:165
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturated"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Saturated: queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or the owner says the runners are full. Stalled: a PR owner has been silent for 2+ hours. Ready: a merge request is in, with green owed CI. Otherwise nothing."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:94
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturation meta-merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:142
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:64
#. Diagram label
msgid "Still holding the lane?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell every sibling and the owner, and update the durable note: either the session that holds the lane now, or that the lane lapses and each session merges its own green PRs with the owner's approval, still sending the six-line merge request."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The loop run by the session that holds the merge-steward lane (actor merge-manager, skill merge-manager-watcher): elected, appointed, or holding it for its own PRs only. Each wake reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and the PR owners live, acknowledges merge requests within the heartbeat, and routes to the train, a direct merge, runner relief, a saturation meta-merge or a stalled-agent takeover. Every merge waits for the owner's own OK, given in the merge manager's session as one card per batch (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B). How a sibling finds or elects the merge manager and sends it a request is Process_MergeRequest."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge manager: the one session holding the merge-steward lane, by the owner's word, by election, or for its own PRs only. Each wake it reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and who owns each PR, acknowledges requests within the heartbeat, then routes to the process the queue needs or stays idle. It hands over explicitly when it stops; like any agent it may stall, and the siblings then re-elect."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:118
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sibling's six lines go into the merge manager's chat first; a request with no rendered preview and no reason goes back to the sibling (owner ruling, 2026-11-07). Then one card per batch, naming each PR, in priority order: P0 main-red fixes and the re-pin chain, P1 work they unblock, P2 CI speed, P3 the rest."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:54
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sweep cadence, as a backstop: every 10-15 minutes while a P0 PR is in flight, every 30 minutes otherwise. Otherwise a subscribed PR event, a sibling's merge request, a main run finishing, or a sibling's message wakes it. Never a polling loop inside a turn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:53
#. Diagram label
msgid "Timer, PR event, request, main run, or sibling message"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:147
#. Diagram label
msgid "Wake handled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "What does the queue need?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:162
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:124
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes for a folio-assistant PR that does not change .github/workflows/. No for a workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Train, A)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:111
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the owner already said to merge this PR when green, so no second card is needed. Otherwise the request goes on the next batch card."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes while the lane is needed (laneNeeded), or while this session manages only its own PRs. No when it stops: the condition no longer holds, or it hands over to a named session."
msgstr ""
